# Collision

The root module owns `golem/collision3d`. `golem/collision`, `collision/cp`, and `collision/resolv` are separate Go modules, developed through the ignored local `go.work`. Test each module explicitly; root `go test ./...` does not cover nested modules.

`collision/layerpolicy` owns name allocation and symmetric masks without importing collision shapes, backends, or the root runtime. The typed 2D and 3D `Layers` facades own backend binding and preserve their diagnostic prefixes and panic order; `Bound()` (nil-safe) lets callers such as the runtime's space transfer reject an unbound facade before `Add`/`Set`/`Remove` would panic. `Bind` stores a typed-nil backend (nil pointer, map, slice, func, chan or interface) as nil, so `Bound()` stays false. `Backend()` (nil-safe) returns the bound backend; the runtime uses it to keep one backend from serving helpers or backends of different spaces. The root module consumes `Layers.Bound` and `Layers.Backend` through the local workspace until the root pin is raised. Define is incremental on failure; matrix changes do not reconfigure already registered shapes. Keep the policy package public because collision3d cannot import collision's internal packages.

`collision/internal/querygeom` owns measured 2D primitive dispatch and narrowphase tests. Chipmunk and resolv own shape extraction and traversal. Chipmunk reads current circle radii/bounding boxes, retains native symmetric query filtering, and selects the nearest cast hit after sorting. Resolv queries original shape dimensions, filters only by layer, and stops at the first map-traversal hit for single-hit casts. Do not normalize these differences or degenerate query encodings during refactors.

Chipmunk reindexes shapes only in `Space.Step`, so `registerBody` and `Update` mark the shape dirty and `OverlapBox`, `OverlapCircle` and `castSegment` flush dirty shapes with `Space.ReindexShape` before their `BBQuery`; `Step` and `Remove` clear entries. Never reindex a locked space (the port has no accessor; `spaceLocked` reads the unexported counter by reflection): queries from Chipmunk callbacks leave shapes dirty. Chipmunk `registerBody` owns shape/filter/sensor creation, space insertion, and bookkeeping. Add creates a kinematic body; AddDynamic owns initial position, mass, and moment. Caller-managed static bodies through Space remain separate.

3D overlap queries share only private traversal. The 2D/3D segment kernels remain distinct: exact-zero checks versus the 3D epsilon, and typed normal construction. Backend methods remain tick-goroutine-only. Contact-event lifecycle and per-space separation belong to the parent runtime and are outside this subsystem: the runtime gives each space its own backend and `Layers` facade, so backends and facades stay unaware of spaces and must not be shared between spaces (the runtime setters panic when one already serves another space, including a backend reached through another space's helper's `Backend()`; `Bound()` and `Lookup` let the runtime validate registrations before space transfers and paired restore publish anything). Shapes a game registers directly on a backend are its own: the runtime moves them only through the game's `SpaceTransfer.MoveShapes` hook, which reaches each space's backend through the runtime's read-only `CollisionBackend` getters; backends need no transfer API.

Release collision with its new helper packages before raising root/cp/resolv dependency pins. A workspace can mask an old published dependency missing those helpers; verify standalone module builds against the intended versions. Never commit local replace directives or workspace files.
